<!--CLI Documentation — UpdateCommand
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation.UpdateCommand-->
<clidocumentation:UpdateCommand xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    blockml update specification
  </is>
  <documentation>
    <![CDATA[
    Syntax:
        blockml update [--no-install]

        The command parses flags, calls clicap:UpdateProject, and prints its
        lines. An unexpected positional argument exits 2 and also prints the
        short USAGE. UpdateProject does not emit USAGE.

        A project is BlockML when package.json has a blockml key. A missing
        package.json, a package.json without that key, or an unreadable
        package.json exits 2 and writes nothing.

        Rewrites @blockml/cli and @blockml/core to the versions of this CLI,
        then runs npm install. @blockml/cli becomes ^ plus this CLI's version.
        @blockml/core becomes the range this CLI depends on. A missing
        @blockml/cli is added under devDependencies. A missing @blockml/core
        is added under dependencies. An entry that already lives in another
        dependency field is updated there. A specifier that contains ":"
        (workspace:, file:, npm:, git, http, …) stays as authored.
        Writes package.json only. BML files, AGENTS.md, and CLAUDE.md stay
        as they are. --no-install skips npm install. Ranges that already
        match exit 0. npm install still runs in that case unless --no-install.

    Printed help:
    Usage: blockml update [--no-install]
           blockml update --help

    When: point an existing BlockML project at the versions of this CLI.

    Rewrites @blockml/cli and @blockml/core in package.json, then runs npm install.
    A project is BlockML when package.json has a blockml key. Otherwise exit 2
    and nothing is written.

    @blockml/cli becomes ^<this CLI version>. @blockml/core becomes the range this
    CLI depends on. A missing @blockml/cli is added in devDependencies. A missing
    @blockml/core is added in dependencies. An entry that already lives in another
    dependency field is updated there. A specifier that contains ":" (workspace:,
    file:, npm:, git, http, …) stays as authored.

    Writes package.json only. BML files, AGENTS.md, and CLAUDE.md stay as they are.
    --no-install skips npm install. Ranges that already match exit 0.
    npm install still runs in that case unless --no-install.

    Run with npx @blockml/cli update so the invoked CLI is the version source.

    Related: init.
    ]]>
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidocumentation:Commands" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clidocumentation:InitCommand" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicap:UpdateProject" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicap:InitProject" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</clidocumentation:UpdateCommand>
